<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/Q86TP1">
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_bf16960d970af7792f5b055fa2cf9e78" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_c3ac981d265cc8fed506239df5ad281a" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_ae727578befb36dac5808549c6f4ce1d" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_642f5e75c19840aa2ef706c182c59a4a" />
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Exopolyphosphatase PRUNE1</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_PRUNE1_identity" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_Q86TP1" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PRUN1_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">DRES-17</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">hPrune</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PRUNE</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PRUNE1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">3.6.1.1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">HTcD37</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Drosophila-related expressed sequence 17</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Protein prune homolog 1</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">DRES17</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PRUN1_HUMAN Reviewed; 453 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference107285</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_58497</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_58497</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Phosphodiesterase (PDE) that has higher activity towardcAMP than cGMP, as substrate. Plays a role in cell proliferation,migration and differentiation, and acts as a negative regulator ofNME1. Plays a role in the regulation of neurogenesis(PubMed:28334956). Involved in the regulation of microtubulepolymerization (PubMed:28334956). {ECO:0000269|PubMed:10602478,ECO:0000269|PubMed:11687967, ECO:0000269|PubMed:14998490,ECO:0000269|PubMed:16428445, ECO:0000269|PubMed:17906697,ECO:0000269|PubMed:28334956}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=diphosphate + H2O = H(+) + 2 phosphate;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:24576, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377, ChEBI:CHEBI:15378,ChEBI:CHEBI:33019, ChEBI:CHEBI:43474; EC=3.6.1.1;COFACTOR:Name=Mn(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:29035; Evidence={ECO:0000250};Note=Binds 2 manganese ions per subunit. {ECO:0000250};ACTIVITY REGULATION: Activated by magnesium ions and inhibited bymanganese ions. Inhibited by dipyridamole, moderately sensitive toIBMX and inhibited by vinpocetine. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:14998490}.BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES:Kinetic parameters:KM=0.91 uM for cAMP {ECO:0000269|PubMed:14998490,ECO:0000269|PubMed:17655525};KM=2.3 uM for cGMP {ECO:0000269|PubMed:14998490,ECO:0000269|PubMed:17655525};Vmax=12.8 pmol/min/ug enzyme with cAMP as substrate{ECO:0000269|PubMed:14998490, ECO:0000269|PubMed:17655525};Vmax=0.8 pmol/min/ug enzyme with cGMP as substrate{ECO:0000269|PubMed:14998490, ECO:0000269|PubMed:17655525};SUBUNIT: Homooligomer. Able to homodimerize via its C-terminaldomain. Interacts with NME1. Interacts with GSK3; at focaladhesion complexes where paxillin and vinculin are colocalized.Interacts with alpha and beta tubulin (PubMed:28334956).{ECO:0000269|PubMed:10602478, ECO:0000269|PubMed:14998490,ECO:0000269|PubMed:16428445, ECO:0000269|PubMed:17655525,ECO:0000269|PubMed:17906697, ECO:0000269|PubMed:28334956}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasm. Nucleus. Cell junction, focaladhesion. Note=In some transfected cells a nuclear staining isalso observed.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=7;Name=1;IsoId=Q86TP1-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=Q86TP1-2; Sequence=VSP_034016;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;Name=3;IsoId=Q86TP1-3; Sequence=VSP_034014;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;Name=4;IsoId=Q86TP1-4; Sequence=VSP_034015, VSP_034017;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;Name=5;IsoId=Q86TP1-5; Sequence=VSP_034014, VSP_034017;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;Name=6;IsoId=Q86TP1-6; Sequence=VSP_034013, VSP_034017;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;Name=7;IsoId=Q86TP1-7; Sequence=VSP_034013;TISSUE SPECIFICITY: Ubiquitously expressed. Seems to beoverexpressed in aggressive sarcoma subtypes, such asleiomyosarcomas and malignant fibrous histiocytomas (MFH) as wellas in the less malignant liposarcomas.{ECO:0000269|PubMed:10602478, ECO:0000269|PubMed:11687967,ECO:0000269|PubMed:15671547}.DISEASE: Neurodevelopmental disorder with microcephaly, hypotonia,and variable brain anomalies (NMIHBA) [MIM:617481]: An autosomalrecessive neurodevelopmental and degenerative disordercharacterized by primary microcephaly, profound globaldevelopmental delay, and severe intellectual disability.Additional clinical features include dysmorphic features, truncalhypotonia, peripheral spasticity, and lack of independentambulation or speech acquisition. Brain imaging shows corticalatrophy, thin corpus callosum, cerebellar hypoplasia, and delayedmyelination. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:26539891,ECO:0000269|PubMed:28211990, ECO:0000269|PubMed:28334956}.Note=The disease is caused by mutations affecting the generepresented in this entry.SIMILARITY: Belongs to the PPase class C family. Prune subfamily.{ECO:0000305}.SEQUENCE CAUTION:Sequence=BAB55423.1; Type=Erroneous initiation; Evidence={ECO:0000305};Sequence=BAG60534.1; Type=Erroneous initiation; Evidence={ECO:0000305}; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_Q86TP1_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/XP_005245450</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_HPRD_15188_identity</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

