<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/P49915">
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_79172a42dcc81881be3eb454654ab89f" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_bb1103f1e111304af83dcf6b9978699b" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_54ac28df7304f1ef79503c2517fd214e" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_c03c892f9d2c4b0f3f05e45557b40774" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_4aeea7765c27a00005c20fc5fdb9331f" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_07ab993d4d301af5b297b343c02fd215" />
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_bea24805f6dc1017353b5c0c11f9b458" />
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GMP synthase [glutamine-hydrolyzing]</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_GMPS_identity" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_P49915" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GUAA_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GMP synthetase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">6.3.5.2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Glutamine amidotransferase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GMPS</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://identifiers.org/refseq/NP_003866</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_uniprotkb_P49915_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference109196</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.phosphosite.org/phosphosite.owl#po_8879</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Involved in the de novo synthesis of guanine nucleotideswhich are not only essential for DNA and RNA synthesis, but alsoprovide GTP, which is involved in a number of cellular processesimportant for cell division.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=ATP + H2O + L-glutamine + XMP = AMP + diphosphate + GMP +2 H(+) + L-glutamate; Xref=Rhea:RHEA:11680, ChEBI:CHEBI:15377,ChEBI:CHEBI:15378, ChEBI:CHEBI:29985, ChEBI:CHEBI:30616,ChEBI:CHEBI:33019, ChEBI:CHEBI:57464, ChEBI:CHEBI:58115,ChEBI:CHEBI:58359, ChEBI:CHEBI:456215; EC=6.3.5.2;PATHWAY: Purine metabolism; GMP biosynthesis; GMP from XMP (L-Glnroute): step 1/1.SUBUNIT: Homodimer. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:23816837}.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasm.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;Name=1;IsoId=P49915-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=P49915-2; Sequence=VSP_053933;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;DISEASE: Note=A chromosomal aberration involving GMPS is found inacute myeloid leukemias. Translocation t(3,11)(q25,q23) withKMT2A/MLL1.WEB RESOURCE: Name=Atlas of Genetics and Cytogenetics in Oncologyand Haematology;URL=&quot;http://atlasgeneticsoncology.org/Genes/GMPSID229.html&quot;; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_8833</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://www.ctdbase.org/#ref_protein_gene_8833</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GUAA_HUMAN Reviewed; 693 AA.</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

<bp:ProteinReference rdf:about="http://identifiers.org/uniprot/P49914">
 <bp:entityFeature rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ModificationFeature_e6695fb4df7c7a32f20ac70a3eae4624" />
 <bp:standardName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">5-formyltetrahydrofolate cyclo-ligase</bp:standardName>
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/RelationshipXref_hgnc_symbol_MTHFS_identity" />
 <bp:xref rdf:resource="http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/UnificationXref_uniprot_knowledgebase_P49914" />
 <bp:organism rdf:resource="http://identifiers.org/taxonomy/9606" />
 <bp:displayName rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MTHFS_HUMAN</bp:displayName>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Methenyl-THF synthetase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">5,10-methenyl-tetrahydrofolate synthetase</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">6.3.3.2</bp:name>
 <bp:name rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MTHFS</bp:name>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_HPRD_10588_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION: Contributes to tetrahydrofolate metabolism. Helpsregulate carbon flow through the folate-dependent one-carbonmetabolic network that supplies carbon for the biosynthesis ofpurines, thymidine and amino acids. Catalyzes the irreversibleconversion of 5-formyltetrahydrofolate (5-FTHF) to yield 5,10-methenyltetrahydrofolate. {ECO:0000269|PubMed:8522195}.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY:Reaction=5-formyltetrahydrofolate + ATP = 5,10-methenyltetrahydrofolate + ADP + phosphate;Xref=Rhea:RHEA:10488, ChEBI:CHEBI:30616, ChEBI:CHEBI:43474,ChEBI:CHEBI:57455, ChEBI:CHEBI:57457, ChEBI:CHEBI:456216;EC=6.3.3.2; Evidence={ECO:0000269|PubMed:8522195};COFACTOR:Name=Mg(2+); Xref=ChEBI:CHEBI:18420;SUBUNIT: Monomer.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION: Cytoplasm.ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS:Event=Alternative splicing; Named isoforms=2;Name=1;IsoId=P49914-1; Sequence=Displayed;Name=2;IsoId=P49914-2; Sequence=VSP_046863;Note=No experimental confirmation available.;SIMILARITY: Belongs to the 5-formyltetrahydrofolate cyclo-ligasefamily. {ECO:0000305}.SEQUENCE CAUTION:Sequence=CK002935; Type=Frameshift; Positions=178, 201; Evidence={ECO:0000305}; COPYRIGHT: UniProt Consortium (www.uniprot.org). Distributed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NoDerivs License.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MTHFS_HUMAN Reviewed; 203 AA.</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://pathwaycommons.org/pc12/ProteinReference_HPRD_09174_identity</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://biocyc.org/biopax/biopax-level3ProteinReference117997</bp:comment>
 <bp:comment rdf:datatype = "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">REPLACED http://mirtarbase.mbc.nctu.edu.tw/#ref_10588</bp:comment>
</bp:ProteinReference>

